.\" Manpage for append_path
.TH append_path 1 "October 26, 2026" "202608311420-git" "append_path"

.SH NAME
append_path

.SH DESCRIPTION
Add directories to PATH. Output is suppressed by default for quiet use in shell startup files. The command cannot modify the environment of its parent shell.

.SH SYNOPSIS
append_path [options] /path/to/dir [path/to/dir ...]

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the full help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display current version.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Create user settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-options
Show all availabe options.
.TP
.B \-\-dir
Change current directory
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Output debugging information.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress normal output. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show normal output.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B append_path --verbose /path/to/dir
Show the result while processing a directory.
.TP
.B append_path --silent /usr/bin/site_perl
Quietly process a directory from a shell startup file.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APPEND_PATH_SILENT
Set to "true" to suppress normal output by default, or "false" to show it. The command-line --silent and --verbose options override this value.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I
~/.config/myscripts/append_path/settings.conf
.TP
.I
/usr/local/bin/append_path

